From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 17:36:40 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vkr: name the failing command when the command stream goes
 fatal

Diagnostic only -- no behaviour change on a healthy stream.

DomA's SurfaceFlinger cannot composite through Venus: its context dies with a
command-stream error, init restarts it, and the screen is corrupted. Measured on
RPi4 hardware 2026-09-08 at 1920x1200 with the display mode matching the
monitor's EDID (so this is not the earlier mode-mismatch defect) -- GL composites
correctly at the same settings, Vulkan does not.

Why the existing logs cannot identify the cause:

  * the reported command name is not evidence past a context's FIRST fault.
    ctx->cs_fatal_error is one non-atomic, never-cleared bool shared by every
    decoder and encoder in the context (vkr_context.h:91, aliased at
    vkr_cs.c:56, vkr_ring.c:135, vkr_context.c:724, sticky per the comment at
    vkr_cs.c:140), and "%s resulted in CS error" tests that shared flag after
    the handler returns.
  * a desync cannot be caught where it happens. The build is -DNDEBUG
    (confirmed in build.ninja for venus_vkr_cs.c.o), so
    vkr_cs_decoder_sanity_check()'s assert(dec->cur <= dec->end) is inert at all
    four of its call sites.
  * only one of the two submit loops was ever instrumented. A capture showed
    both "ring_submit_cmd: vn_dispatch_command failed" (vkr_ring.c) and
    "submit_cmd: vn_dispatch_command failed" (vkr_context.c, the direct path).

This adds, in that order: a shared logging helper, the pre-dispatch cursor in
BOTH submit loops, and one live sanity condition.

The helper checks its bounds before touching anything, and that is not defensive
padding. cmd_begin is not necessarily inside [buffer, buffer + size):
vkExecuteCommandStreamsMESA repoints the decoder at a resource via
vkr_cs_decoder_set_resource_stream(), so the next iteration of the loop starts
inside that resource. Computing cmd_begin - buffer without the check and reading
through it kills the render server -- measured as "proxy: failed to send
message: Broken pipe" with no dump line printed at all.

What the capture already told us without the dump, and why it is worth having:
the failing lookup was

    vkr: failed to look up object 4294967307 of type 6
    vkr: vkCmdDraw resulted in CS error

type 6 is VK_OBJECT_TYPE_COMMAND_BUFFER and 4294967307 is 0x1_0000_000B -- the
low dword is a plausible small object id (11) with a stray 1 in the high dword.
A guest that encoded a handle would encode a valid id, so garbage in the upper
half points at a shifted 64-bit read, i.e. a real cursor desync rather than the
guest sending a wrong-but-valid handle. The dump is what turns that inference
into a measurement: the byte offset and the leading bytes say whether the shift
is 4 or 8 bytes and what the neighbouring word was.

The live condition is dec->cur running past dec->end. It fires at the
divergence, before any object lookup, so its presence or absence in the next
capture separates a genuine desync from a bad handle. It is done as an explicit
check rather than by dropping -DNDEBUG globally, because that would also re-arm
vkr_context.h's duplicate-object-id assert and abort the render server on a
condition the release build tolerates today.

Ruled out from source before writing this, so they are not re-tried: the
decoder, its cursor and its temp pool are per-ring, not per-context
(vkr_ring.h:89, vkr_cs.h:81-82, vkr_ring.c:214), and one thread drives each
ring, so two rings cannot corrupt each other's stream position; the ring wrap
arithmetic mirrors the guest's write split (vkr_ring.c:84-101 against Mesa's
vn_ring.c:126-140); the temp pool cap is 1 GiB; and the direct path copies the
whole pending range into a private buffer before decoding. VN_PERF=no_multi_ring
does not prevent the failure, and the commands seen failing (vkCmdDraw,
vkAllocateDescriptorSets, vkCreateImageView, vkCmdCopyBufferToImage) all travel
the primary ring, which is consistent with multi-ring not being the mechanism.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [diagnostic instrumentation]
---
--- a/src/venus/vkr_ring.c
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_ring.c
@@ -220,9 +220,13 @@
    vkr_cs_decoder_set_buffer_stream(dec, buffer, size);
 
    while (vkr_cs_decoder_has_command(dec)) {
+      const uint8_t *cmd_begin = dec->cur;
       vn_dispatch_command(&ring->dispatch);
       if (vkr_cs_decoder_get_fatal(dec)) {
          vkr_log("ring_submit_cmd: vn_dispatch_command failed");
+         vkr_log("ring_submit_cmd: ring %" PRIu64 " ctx %u ring_head=%u", ring->id,
+                 ((const struct vkr_context *)ring->dispatch.data)->ctx_id, ring_head);
+         vkr_cs_decoder_log_fatal_cmd(dec, "ring_submit_cmd", buffer, size, cmd_begin);
 
          vkr_cs_decoder_reset(dec);
          return false;
--- a/src/venus/vkr_cs.c
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_cs.c
@@ -104,6 +104,21 @@
       assert(pool->cur <= pool->end);
    }
 
+   /* Make just this one condition live. It is checked from four call sites and
+    * fires AT the divergence, before any object lookup -- which is what tells a
+    * real cursor desync apart from the guest having encoded a bad handle while
+    * the cursor was still correct.
+    *
+    * Deliberately NOT done by dropping -DNDEBUG globally: that would also
+    * re-arm vkr_context.h's duplicate-object-id assert and abort the render
+    * server on a condition the release build tolerates today.
+    */
+   if (unlikely(dec->cur > dec->end)) {
+      vkr_log("cs sanity: cur %p is %zu bytes past end %p", (const void *)dec->cur,
+              (size_t)(dec->cur - dec->end), (const void *)dec->end);
+      vkr_cs_decoder_set_fatal(dec);
+   }
+
    assert(dec->cur <= dec->end);
 }
 
--- a/src/venus/vkr_cs.h
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_cs.h
@@ -227,6 +227,51 @@
    dec->end = dec->cur + size;
 }
 
+/* Diagnostic for the two submit loops. The shipped build is -DNDEBUG, so
+ * vkr_cs_decoder_sanity_check()'s assert(dec->cur <= dec->end) is inert and a
+ * stream desync is only noticed later, as a garbage object lookup naming a
+ * command that was never at fault. Print where the offending command actually
+ * started and what its bytes were.
+ *
+ * cmd_begin is NOT necessarily inside [buffer, buffer + size): a command such
+ * as vkExecuteCommandStreamsMESA repoints the decoder at a resource through
+ * vkr_cs_decoder_set_resource_stream(), and the next iteration of the submit
+ * loop then starts inside that resource instead. Dereferencing it against the
+ * buffer without a bounds check kills the render server (measured: "proxy:
+ * failed to send message: Broken pipe" with no dump line), so the bounds are
+ * checked before any pointer arithmetic or read.
+ */
+static inline void
+vkr_cs_decoder_log_fatal_cmd(const struct vkr_cs_decoder *dec,
+                             const char *tag,
+                             const uint8_t *buffer,
+                             size_t size,
+                             const uint8_t *cmd_begin)
+{
+   if (!cmd_begin || cmd_begin < buffer || cmd_begin >= buffer + size) {
+      vkr_log("%s: fatal on a non-buffer stream (cmd_begin %p outside [%p,%p)); "
+              "the decoder had been repointed at a resource",
+              tag, (const void *)cmd_begin, (const void *)buffer,
+              (const void *)(buffer + size));
+      return;
+   }
+
+   const size_t off = (size_t)(cmd_begin - buffer);
+   size_t n = size - off;
+   if (n > 32)
+      n = 32;
+   char hex[32 * 3 + 1];
+   for (size_t i = 0; i < n; i++)
+      snprintf(hex + i * 3, 4, "%02x ", cmd_begin[i]);
+   hex[n ? n * 3 - 1 : 0] = 0;
+
+   const uint8_t *cur = dec->cur;
+   const size_t consumed =
+      (cur >= cmd_begin && cur <= buffer + size) ? (size_t)(cur - cmd_begin) : 0;
+   vkr_log("%s: chunk=%zu cmd_off=%zu consumed=%zu bytes=[%s]", tag, size, off,
+           consumed, hex);
+}
+
 bool
 vkr_cs_decoder_set_resource_stream(struct vkr_cs_decoder *dec,
                                    struct vkr_context *ctx,
--- a/src/venus/vkr_context.c
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_context.c
@@ -170,9 +170,13 @@
    vkr_cs_decoder_set_buffer_stream(&ctx->decoder, buffer, size);
 
    while (vkr_cs_decoder_has_command(&ctx->decoder)) {
+      const uint8_t *cmd_begin = ctx->decoder.cur;
       vn_dispatch_command(&ctx->dispatch);
       if (vkr_context_get_fatal(ctx)) {
          vkr_log("submit_cmd: vn_dispatch_command failed");
+         vkr_log("submit_cmd: ctx %u (direct path, no ring)", ctx->ctx_id);
+         vkr_cs_decoder_log_fatal_cmd(&ctx->decoder, "submit_cmd", buffer, size,
+                                      cmd_begin);
 
          vkr_cs_decoder_reset(&ctx->decoder);
          return false;
